# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Heavy, regenerable artifacts (never in Git)
# (cache features live in cache/ and are *.npz, so no broad "features/" pattern --
#  that would also ignore the src/luq/features/ source code.)
hf_cache/
saved_outputs/
cache/
results/
logs/
*.pt
*.npz

# Scheduler job logs: PBS/Slurm write <jobname>.o<jobid> / .e<jobid> stdout+stderr
# into the submit dir. Regenerable console output, never source -- ignore them.
*.o[0-9]*
*.e[0-9]*

# Transient scheduler bookkeeping written by the job-watcher shell loops: bare lists of PBS job
# IDs, and a zero-byte "fleet launched" sentinel. Five of these were committed by accident and
# untracked on 2026-08-14. The job IDs are long dead and document nothing reproducible.
.luq_*
.seg_fleet_launched

# Secrets
.env

# macOS
.DS_Store

# PBS job logs (persistent by design -- see pbs/topk_prior_one_eval.pbs -- but not artifacts to track)
logs/

# The worktree's cache is a SYMLINK to the main checkout's cache, so the existing 'cache/'
# pattern (which matches directories) never matched it and it sat untracked forever. A permanently
# dirty 'git status' is not cosmetic here: the untracked-file sweep in CLAUDE.md relies on it.
cache

# `results` is now a SYMLINK to ../results, i.e. into the PRIVATE PARENT repo, which is where the
# result files are version-controlled from 2026-08-14 (they previously sat in no repository at all).
# The code keeps reading and writing `results/...` exactly as before, because this path still
# resolves -- that is the entire point of the symlink, and it is why no driver, PBS script or glob
# needed changing. Same trailing-slash trap as `cache` above: the 'results/' pattern on line 12
# matches a DIRECTORY and does NOT match this symlink, so the bare form is required or the tree
# reads permanently dirty and the CLAUDE.md untracked sweep stops working.
results

# ---- INTERNAL GUIDANCE DOCS DO NOT BELONG IN THE SUBMITTED REPO (rule added 2026-08-08) ----
# This repo is the submitted artifact and should read as a record of what was actually RUN.
# Agent briefs, session hand-overs and "how to find your bearings" explainers are INTERNAL: they
# belong in the PRIVATE parent (private_luq) beside CLAUDE.md and the plans. Anything mentioning
# Claude/an assistant especially so. Pre-registrations and analysis scripts are NOT in this class --
# they are part of the record and stay tracked here.
*_BRIEF_*.md
DOC_BRIEF*.md
DOC_INSTRUCTIONS.md
AGENT_*.md
*_HANDOVER*.md

# Agent scratch / worktrees. INTERNAL by definition (see CLAUDE.md: internal guidance never goes
# in the submitted repo). A 42MB unlabelled records duplicate was found here on 2026-08-11, untracked
# but NOT ignored, so a `git add -A` would have swept it into the submitted artifact.
.claude/
